# M31 fixture mom_federation_lifecycle — observer golden.
# expected.observer.log
# attestation: spec-derived from IEEE 1516.1-2010 references below
# Cross-check status: NOT CROSS-CHECKED — fixture uses >2 federates; exceeds the scope of the locally licensed validation environment. Independently verifiable against any DLC-conformant RTI via the external commercial-RTI harness. See docs/COMMERCIAL_RTI_PARITY.md.
# canonicalization: cppsdk/tests/dlc/conformance/_harness/normalize.py
# spec-cites: see README.md
#
# M36 amendments to the M31 skeleton (see README "M36 DD re-verdict"):
#  1. Instance names: the skeleton expected `name=HLAfederate` for all three
#     instances, but IEEE 1516.1-2010 §6.2 requires object instance names to
#     be UNIQUE — three identical names are unrealizable on any conforming
#     RTI. RTI-assigned names are `HLAfederate.<federateHandle>` (commercial-RTI-style
#     convention); the harness normalizes the handle suffix
#     (`name=HLAfederate.<H>`) per the same §5.2.1 policy as bare handle ints.
#  2. REMOVE position: the skeleton put alice's REMOVE after bob's lines,
#     contradicting both its own comment ("alice resigns first") and the
#     driver sequencing (alice joins+resigns BEFORE bob starts). Causal
#     stream order per §6 places alice's REMOVE before bob's DISCOVER.
#  3. Added bob's REMOVE: bob also resigns (CANCEL_THEN_DELETE_THEN_DIVEST)
#     while the observer is still pumping callbacks, so his HLAfederate
#     instance removal is observed too (§6.15) — the skeleton missed it.
OBS: CONNECT                                                       # §4.2
OBS: JOIN federate=observer                                        # §4.9 — observer joins first
OBS: SUBSCRIBE class=HLAobjectRoot.HLAmanager.HLAfederate attributes=[HLAfederateHandle,HLAfederateName] active=true  # §5.6 + §11 standard MOM path (catalogue 16.1 — no bespoke API)
OBS: DISCOVER name=HLAfederate.<H>                                 # §11 — RTI publishes per-federate MOM object; late subscriber retro-discovers its own record; §6.9 (catalogue 4.19 wstring)
OBS: REFLECT HLAfederateName=observer                              # §11 — MOM populates name attribute via standard reflectAttributeValues RO (catalogue 4.20)
OBS: DISCOVER name=HLAfederate.<H>
OBS: REFLECT HLAfederateName=alice
OBS: REMOVE                                                        # §6.15 removeObjectInstance (catalogue 4.22) — alice resigns; MOM removes her HLAfederate object
OBS: DISCOVER name=HLAfederate.<H>
OBS: REFLECT HLAfederateName=bob
OBS: REMOVE                                                        # §6.15 — bob resigns while the observer is still pumping
OBS: RESIGN action=CANCEL_THEN_DELETE_THEN_DIVEST                  # §4.10
